From 17b53d034a7af46b56e0e2104ee742a930047809 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ohgur <ohgurlabs@github.com>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 15:11:22 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 8/9] hip-tests: add hipGraphExecUpdate error-propagation
 regression test

Unit_hipGraphExecUpdate_ExhaustionErrorPropagation asserts the contract this
PR restores: under kernel-argument exhaustion, hipGraphExecUpdate fails as
hipErrorGraphExecUpdateFailure with hErrorNode_out and updateResult_out set
(never hipSuccess with a stale packet); iterations that report success verify
the freshly-updated value; and destroy + re-instantiate recovers, with the
subsequent update + launch verifying (the framework fallback pattern this
error code enables, e.g. ggml's).

Companion to Unit_hipGraphExecUpdate_KernargPoolExhaustion (PR #10022): that
test asserts no-crash/no-corruption; this one asserts the specific error
surface and the recovery path. Logic validated standalone on gfx1100
(therock-7.14 + this patch): clean failure with errorNode set, and 25
consecutive destroy/re-instantiate recovery cycles, 102,600 verified
bit-exact launches at 0 MiB free.

Related: #10021, #10713
